# 1-based lines to bookmark, one per line.
#
# Bash has no type or module layer, so the deepest breadcrumb this language can
# produce is `function > statement`. Each line below sits inside a different
# control-flow kind, so a wrong `containers` shows up as a missing breadcrumb
# rather than passing unnoticed.

# Inside the `if` in resolve_target() — the breadcrumb must name the function.
38

# Inside a `case` branch in resolve_target(). `case_statement` is labelled but
# must NOT be a container: the breadcrumb names the function, not the branch.
#
# This targets the branch's `local` declaration rather than its `printf`. A bare
# command inside a case branch cannot be bookmarked at all: `case_item` is not a
# landmark, so the query has no anchor between the command and the function, and
# a lone `(command)` pattern matches every `printf` in the file. Picking a
# `declaration_command` gives the query something to anchor on. Same class of
# generator limitation as codemark#239.
50

# Inside the `if` inside the `for` in upload_artifacts() — two statement levels,
# so the breadcrumb walk has to skip both to find the function.
68

# Inside the `while` body in verify_checksums().
94

# Inside the `until` loop — Bash models `until` as a keyword token inside
# `while_statement`, so this exercises the same kind from the other spelling.
99

# Inside the `if` in main().
120
